Bannerlator linuxfs (tools/linuxfs/turnip), 2026-09-20.
The two KGSL fixes the Linux runtime needs, both device-proven there:

kgsl-drm-node.patch
  KGSL exposes no DRM render node, so Turnip reported no DRM device and a Wayland
  compositor's dma-buf feedback and the WSI could not agree on a main device.
  Reports /dev/kgsl-3d0's own major:minor as local and master, and lets
  VK_EXT_physical_device_drm advertise when it is known.

kgsl-no-calibrated-timestamps.patch
  kgsl cannot read the GPU counter (kgsl_device_get_gpu_timestamp was
  UNREACHABLE("")), yet VK_KHR/EXT_calibrated_timestamps and VK_EXT_present_timing
  were advertised from has_persistent_counter alone - so a compositor that used
  them aborted the process. Gates all three on the kernel interface actually
  implementing the call. Ported from Max's fix.

kgsl-syncobj-merge-ts-fd.patch (DroidDeck, 2026-09-26; still in Mesa main)
  kgsl_syncobj_merge converted the wrong syncobj when a timestamp result met a
  sync-file: it called kgsl_syncobj_ts_to_fd on the fd syncobj, which has no queue
  (NULL dereference in release builds, an assert in debug ones), and the
  two-queues branch merged an fd the timestamp result never had. A submit that
  waits on two semaphores of the two kinds - Cemu's every frame: the previous
  command buffer plus the swapchain acquire - crashed on the first frame. Now the
  timestamp side becomes the fence and is merged with the fd.
